extraStrings:
- type: en-US
  strings: &id001
    STR_RUMOURED_TERROR_GROUP: A Rumoured Terror Group
    STR_RUMOURED_TERROR_GROUP_UFOPEDIA: 'Hawk''s first briefing. For a year the agencies have traded rumours of a new terrorist organisation: well armed, well paid, and nowhere when anyone goes to look.
      Nobody has a name for it. Nobody has a photograph.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We start where the guns are. A cartel on the Texas border has been fielding hardware it should not be able to buy.'
    STR_CARTEL_LEDGER: Cartel Ledger
    STR_CARTEL_LEDGER_UFOPEDIA: 'The cartel boss kept his own books in his own safe. Most of it is drugs and bribes. One supplier stands out: no name, cash in advance, and pickups from an old weapons plant
      in West Texas that closed years ago.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}A closed factory does not sell rifles. Somebody is using it.'
    STR_CRATE_SERIAL_PLATE: Crate Serial Plate
    STR_CRATE_SERIAL_PLATE_UFOPEDIA: Roadblock traced the serial plate off a crate in the barn. The number belongs to no army and no maker on any register. The only match is a lot number stamped at the
      same West Texas plant the ledger names.
    STR_COBRA_STENCIL: Cobra Stencil
    STR_COBRA_STENCIL_UFOPEDIA: 'Painted on the inside lid of a crate where nobody was meant to see it: a coiled snake, hood spread. It means nothing to anyone in The Pit yet.'
    STR_WHO_IS_COBRA: Who Is Cobra?
    STR_WHO_IS_COBRA_UFOPEDIA: The snake on the crates and the money in the ledger belong to the same people. They call themselves Cobra. From now on, anything we take from them goes to the lab.
    STR_CARTEL_BOSS_INTERROGATION: Cartel Boss Interrogation
    STR_CARTEL_BOSS_INTERROGATION_UFOPEDIA: 'The boss is a businessman and bargains like one. His supplier warned him off the West Texas plant for a while: new owners were coming, and they would want it
      back on a fixed date. He tells us the date.'
    STR_FACTORY_SCHEDULE: Factory Production Schedule
    STR_FACTORY_SCHEDULE_UFOPEDIA: 'Found in the plant manager''s office: a production schedule on paper headed with the snake. Lines restart, guards arrive and the first shipment leaves on a date that
      is now circled on Hawk''s calendar.'
    STR_FACTORY_REACTIVATION_DATE: Factory Reactivation Date
    STR_FACTORY_REACTIVATION_DATE_UFOPEDIA: We know when Cobra takes the West Texas plant back. Hit it before then and production never starts. Hit it on the day and it will be guarded. Leave it, and the
      rifles it makes will turn up in Cobra hands within months.
    STR_TRACE_THE_BROADCAST: Trace the Broadcast
    STR_TRACE_THE_BROADCAST_UFOPEDIA: 'Cobra Commander has spoken to the world: a hooded man, a snake banner and a threat. Breaker took the signal apart. It was relayed three times, but the first relay
      was careless, and it leads to one building where a Cobra cell is waiting.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}It is a cell, not a headquarters. It is a start.'
    STR_EXTENSIVE_ENTERPRISES: Extensive Enterprises
    STR_EXTENSIVE_ENTERPRISES_UFOPEDIA: 'The money in Cobra''s books runs through one company: Extensive Enterprises, owned on paper by twin brothers, Tomax and Xamot Paoli. It has warehouses, shipping
      lines and offices in three countries, and every one of them is legal on paper.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Cobra''s money moves through these businesses. Their warehouses and offices can now be raided.'
    STR_MAJOR_BLUDD: Major Bludd
    STR_MAJOR_BLUDD_UFOPEDIA: 'Sebastian Bludd: mercenary, poet of sorts, and now Cobra''s. He left a calling card with the names of the Joes who stopped him, and a promise in verse that he will see each
      of them again.'
    STR_SHIPPING_MANIFEST: Shipping Manifest
    STR_SHIPPING_MANIFEST_UFOPEDIA: A manifest for a cargo that does not exist, from a company that does not trade, to a warehouse that keeps appearing in other papers.
    STR_PILOT_LOGBOOK: Pilot's Logbook
    STR_PILOT_LOGBOOK_UFOPEDIA: 'A Cobra pilot''s logbook: times, fuel and landing strips, written in a private shorthand that Scarlett can read.'
    STR_DEPOT_ROUTE_ANALYSIS: Depot Route Analysis
    STR_DEPOT_ROUTE_ANALYSIS_UFOPEDIA: 'Put the manifests, the logbook, the fuel receipts and the bills of lading on one map and the same places come up again and again. Without a Cobra officer to confirm
      it this took longer, but the answer is the same: depots.'
    STR_COBRA_DEPOTS: Cobra Depots
    STR_COBRA_DEPOTS_UFOPEDIA: 'Cobra''s flights and trucks do not run cell to cell. They run to depots: warehouses where guns, money and men are gathered and sent on. Depots can now be found, and a depot
      found can be raided.'
    STR_DEPOT_RECORDS: Depot Records
    STR_DEPOT_RECORDS_UFOPEDIA: Records from a raided Cobra depot. Most of the stock went out to the cells. A share of everything went somewhere else.
    STR_TERROR_DROME_RUMOURS: Rumours of a Terror Drome
    STR_TERROR_DROME_RUMOURS_UFOPEDIA: Every depot sends a share of its stock to the same place, and none of our sources has seen it. Prisoners call it the Drome. They describe a fortress with its own air
      wing, and they say it is nearly finished.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}How far along it is can now be read from captured documents.
    STR_TERROR_DROME_PLANS: Terror Drome Defense Plans
    STR_TERROR_DROME_PLANS_UFOPEDIA: 'The defense plans of Cobra''s first Terror Drome: gun positions, the Firebat launch bay, the garrison rota and the location. Hawk is drawing up the assault.'
    STR_MARS_MARKINGS: M.A.R.S. Markings
    STR_MARS_MARKINGS_UFOPEDIA: 'Roadblock found it on a rifle from the Drome, under Cobra''s paint: a maker''s mark. M.A.R.S., Military Armaments Research Syndicate. Cobra does not build its own weapons.
      Somebody sells them, and he has a name.'
    STR_CARTEL_BOSS: Cartel Boss
    STR_BROADCAST_RECORDING: Broadcast Recording
    STR_BLUDD_CALLING_CARD: Bludd's Calling Card
    STR_MARS_MARKED_WEAPON: M.A.R.S.-Marked Weapon
- type: en-GB
  strings: *id001
